NOTE (plan 11-08 refresh, 2026-10-10, on the tree after the Phase 11 review fixes).
Command: SOAK_DURATION_MS=60000 SOAK_WRITE_INTERVAL_MS=250 npm run soak   (3 server processes by default; D-14 env knobs)
The DEFAULT soak (3 processes, 120 s, 100 ms write interval) is NOT used on this host: every write audits EVERY row
of each collection it touches (O(N) audit rows per write), so it filled the disk with a 5.5 GB audit.db and died with
SQLITE_FULL (11-08-SUMMARY.md finding F-5, identical on the pre-Phase-11 tree; Phase 12 scope). The verdict below is
the same script at a lighter rate and a 60 s window.
A first run on this tree reported "every acknowledged write present and exact: mismatched=1842" with missing=0. That
was the HARNESS, not the server: since review fix IN-02 a real deal stamps a pulse's employeeName from the signed-in
account and ignores the body value (test/personal-data-reads.test.js), and scripts/soak.js carried its per-write
correlator in employeeName, so (a) the "exact" comparison could not match and (b) the "a 503 left nothing committed"
lookup, which also keyed on employeeName, would have passed vacuously. scripts/soak.js now carries the correlator in
`comment` (stored verbatim) and compares rating / comment / type; nothing else in the script changed. This run is the
re-run with that harness fix.
